  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can find the unit of acceleration by substituting the given units of force and mass into the formula and simplifying.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{F}{m} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}})}{\\text{kg}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{kg}}\\,\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}\\,\\cancel{\\text{kg}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the unit of acceleration is $\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
